{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775347866-4sgNf4uqzzglZ95TcOOd","role":"assistant","created":1775347873,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the structure better. Let me search for the December 18, 1952 issue in the Offerings table to understand which treasury bills correspond to which dates. The Market Quotations table shows outstanding amounts as of January 30, 1953 for treasury bills that were issued on various dates.\n\nFrom the Market Quotations (Table 1), I can see:\n- Issue date 10/3/52: Amount outstanding = $2,502 million\n- Issue date 12/19/52: Amount outstanding = $1,200 million\n\nBut I need to find the one with issue date 12/18/52. Let me look more carefully at the Offerings table to see all December 1952 dates.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_43975f766bdf4afe8331750d","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport json, re\n\n# Load data from file\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1953_03.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\nelements = data['document']['elements']\n\n# Get the Offerings of Treasury Bills table\ntable_elem = elements[296]\ncontent = table_elem.get('content', '')\n\n# Let's see all entries in this table - find rows with Dec. 18\n# The table shows the full offering details\nrows = content.split('<tr>')\nprint(\"All December 1952 treasury bill offerings:\")\nfor row in rows:\n    if 'Dec.' in row:\n        # Extract issue date and amount\n        # Format: td>Dec. X.</td><td>...\n        match = re.search(r'<td>([^<]+Dec[^<]*)</td>', row)\n        if match:\n            print(f\"Issue: {match.group(1)}\")\n        # Extract the amount of bids accepted (column 5)\n        amounts = re.findall(r'<td>([0-9,]+\\.[0-9]+)</td>', row)\n        if amounts:\n            print(f\"  Amounts: {amounts}\")\n        print()\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
