{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775347906-IHWBqjkiX5EEQ50PyZoy","role":"assistant","created":1775347915,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The December 18, 1952 treasury bill was issued for $1,200 million (as shown in the Offerings table). This is now confirmed.\n\nSo the answer is:\n- October 3, 1952 issue: $2,502 million \n- December 18, 1952 issue: $1,200 million\n- Absolute difference: 1,302 million\n\nLet me verify by double checking the Market Quotations table again to confirm both values are in \"Amount outstanding (millions)\" column for those specific issue dates:\n\nActually wait - I need to confirm that the $2,502 million shown in the Market Quotations table for the 10/3/52 issue is indeed the total outstanding amount. Let me verify this.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_8473fbf5cb584b929f0d3601","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport json, re\n\n# Load data from file\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1953_03.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\nelements = data['document']['elements']\n\n# Get the Market Quotations table (Table 1)\ntable_elem = elements[515]\ncontent = table_elem.get('content', '')\n\n# The table has two columns side by side. Let me extract both properly\n# Looking at the raw HTML to understand the structure better\n\n# First, let's see what we have for the 10/3/52 and 12/18/52 entries\n# Based on the table structure:\n# Left column: Amount | Maturity | Issue date | Bid | Ask | Mean | Change\n# Right column: Amount | Maturity | Issue date | Bid | Ask | Mean | Change\n\nprint(\"Parsing Market Quotations table for Treasury Bills (Taxable):\")\nprint(\"=\"*60)\n\n# The table is in a specific format\n# Let's extract the left side first - it has the amounts for bills issued before this period\n# And the right side has additional bills\n\n# Let's look at each row\nrows = content.split('</tr>')\nfor row in rows:\n    if '10/3/52' in row:\n        print(\"\\nRow with 10/3/52:\")\n        # Get all the td values\n        cells = re.findall(r'<td[^>]*>([^<]+)</td>', row)\n        print(f\"Cells: {cells}\")\n        \n    if '12/18/52' in row:\n        print(\"\\nRow with 12/18/52:\")\n        cells = re.findall(r'<td[^>]*>([^<]+)</td>', row)\n        print(f\"Cells: {cells}\")\n        \n    if '12/19/52' in row:\n        print(\"\\nRow with 12/19/52:\")\n        cells = re.findall(r'<td[^>]*>([^<]+)</td>', row)\n        print(f\"Cells: {cells}\")\n        \nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*60)\nprint(\"Summary from Market Quotations table (as of Jan 30, 1953):\")\nprint(\"  Issue date 10/3/52: Amount outstanding = $2,502 million\")\nprint(\"  Issue date 12/19/52: Amount outstanding = $1,200 million\")\nprint(\"\\nBut there's NO 12/18/52 entry in Market Quotations table\")\nprint(\"\\nFrom Offerings table:\")\nprint(\"  Issue date 12/18/52: Amount issued = $1,200 million\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
